  "kind": "bit-matching-detail",
  "title": "IMDIV scales by the larger denominator component and flushes subnormal output components below DBL_MIN to 0",
  "statement": "In Excel 16.0 builds 20430 and 20527, IMDIV(inumber1, inumber2) returns #NUM! for a 0+0i divisor, scales both numerator and denominator by ratio = im2/re2 (when |re2| >= |im2|) or re2/im2 to avoid overflow/underflow, and flushes any real or imaginary quotient below DBL_MIN to 0 before complex text assembly. All 2,067 full-bank IMDIV rows match.",
  "status": "measured",
  "basis": "Measured in CalcFunc-Evidence runs/w111-complex-kernels-20260929/answers/answers-imdiv.json.gz (Excel 16.0 build 20430) and Excel 16.0.20527.20088 (jnt_parity_complex row 594); 2,067/2,067 full-bank rows match.",
